From 1769fd956bf5bf0d6d3bc44b95a175945bf31871 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivy Evans <ivy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:48:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Controller: drive the swoop race and the turret from the
 pad

The swoop and the Ebon Hawk's turret did not respond to the pad at all.
ProcessInput (0x00623F48) builds their control vector from the keyboard's
class-1 axis events alone, (0x11E + 0x11B, 0, 0) for the swoop and
(0x11E + 0x11B, 0, 0x11D + 0x11A) for the turret, and passes it to
CSWMiniGame's input step at 0x00670FB0; fire is events 0xD9 (Space) and
0x19 (the left mouse button), which the action router sends to the
player's fire at 0x0066DC50. Every one of those ids already holds a
keyboard or mouse description, one per id, so none can be bound to the
pad, and the module's own axes, though added to class 1, are polled by
nothing there.

Hook the input step instead. The left stick fills an axis the keyboard
leaves at zero, and fire follows the Xbox manual: A in the swoop (the
thrusters, then each gear shift), either trigger on the turret, edge-
triggered as a key press is and behind the router's own guard. The
keyboard and the mouse are unchanged.

Read from the executable decrypted in memory. Played in a swoop race:
the stick steers the way it is pushed and A starts and shifts. The
turret has not been played.
